  "question": {
    "text": "A parallel plate capacitor with plate area A and plate separation $d=2 \\mathrm{~m}$ has a capacitance of $4 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$.\nThe new capacitance of the system if half of the space between them is filled with a dielectric material of dielectric constant $\\mathrm{K}=3$ (as shown in figure) will be:\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/gnNODDb46rlSYm79fYRjnQTl5L8pmrwgZaF9dr7NDfc.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NtFor",
      "text": "$2 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sgw73",
      "text": "$32 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "X6SZ5",
      "text": "$6 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SQi7K",
      "text": "$8 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $C_i=\\frac{A \\epsilon_0}{d}=4 \\mu F$\n$C_f=\\frac{A \\epsilon_0}{d-t+\\frac{t}{k}}=\\frac{A \\epsilon_0}{d-\\frac{d}{2}+\\frac{d}{2 \\times 3}}$\n$=\\frac{A \\in_0}{d\\left(1-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}\\right)}$\n$=\\frac{4 \\mu F}{\\frac{2}{3}}=6 \\mu F$",
    "image": null
  },
